# SEO Rules — Public Marketplace Pages

"Compare housing societies in [city]" and similar queries are a real,
currently-unserved search opportunity for this product. SEO here is a
ranking-system requirement, not decoration — treat it as such.

## Every new public page

- Implements `generateMetadata` with a unique, descriptive title and
  description derived from the actual entity data (society name, city,
  category) — never a generic static title reused across pages.
- Has a corresponding entry in `sitemap.ts` if it represents a real,
  crawlable entity (society, category, dealer profile). If you add a new
  entity type intended to be publicly discoverable, update the sitemap
  generator in the same change.
- Sets a `canonical` URL — for the comparison tool specifically, the
  canonical points to the page's own URL (each parameter combination is a
  legitimate distinct page, not duplicate content to be canonicalized away).

## Structured data (JSON-LD)

- Society pages emit `Organization` schema; inventory categories emit
  `RealEstateListing` schema with `priceRange`/`availability`; pages with
  reviews emit `AggregateRating`; all pages emit `BreadcrumbList`.
- Use the shared `packages/ui/seo/JsonLd.tsx` component with a
  Zod-validated schema object — don't hand-write a `<script>` tag with
  inline JSON per page.
- Validate new structured data against Google's Rich Results Test before
  considering the page done — a schema that's present but malformed is
  worse than none, since it can trigger a manual action.

## Rendering strategy

- `/societies` directory: SSR, filters as URL search params (so filtered
  views are crawlable/shareable, not client-state-only).
- `/societies/[city]/[society]`: ISR with a 6-hour revalidation window —
  don't switch this to fully dynamic rendering without a specific reason,
  since inventory counts changing slightly doesn't require always-fresh HTML.
- Heavy interactive widgets (the comparison tool) are dynamically imported
  (`next/dynamic`) so they don't bloat the initial page bundle for users
  who are just browsing.

## Core Web Vitals

- `next/image` with explicit dimensions for every image; `next/font` for
  all fonts. A public page shipped without these is not done — Lighthouse
  SEO + Performance should be ≥ 90 before merging.
